WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.272
C++ 26 is

00:00:02.083 --> 00:00:03.180
finished for the

00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:03.923
second time

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:06.356
C++ 26 was

00:00:06.168 --> 00:00:07.287
first completed in

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:07.712
March

00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:09.021
but its international

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.035
approval ballot did

00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:11.250
not pass unanimously

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.665
mostly over concerns

00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:13.537
about contracts

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:15.052
At a six-day

00:00:14.864 --> 00:00:16.102
meeting in Búzios

00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:16.679
Brazil

00:00:16.786 --> 00:00:18.401
with about 220

00:00:18.213 --> 00:00:19.899
attendees from 27

00:00:19.711 --> 00:00:20.429
nations

00:00:20.595 --> 00:00:21.821
the committee extended

00:00:21.633 --> 00:00:22.411
contracts

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:24.085
explained its decisions

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.229
and finished the

00:00:25.041 --> 00:00:26.420
technical work again

00:00:26.942 --> 00:00:28.215
The updated standard

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:28.899
now heads to

00:00:28.711 --> 00:00:29.748
a second ballot

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:30.762
and the committee

00:00:30.586 --> 00:00:32.024
also adopted labeled

00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:33.074
break and continue

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.300
and views slice

00:00:34.418 --> 00:00:36.222
for C++ 29

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:37.764
Full story on

00:00:37.575 --> 00:00:38.471
the dashboard
